    {
      "type": "len_string",
      "start": 821,
      "end": 838,
      "length": 15,
      "text": "\u0000\u0000\u00ec\u00ffw\u0000\u0094\u0001After t"
    },
    {
      "type": "ascii",
      "start": 838,
      "end": 1235,
      "text": "he exile of the Wolf Clan, and their retreat to Arc-Royal, Khan Phelan Kell ordered the clansmen to work with the Kell Hounds and the Wolf Dragoons to create better weapons and equipment based off of existing designs and upon their success, his Mech that was rebuilt by Ulric Kerensky was refitted with the new weapons which were lighter and more powerful giving him a decidely more powerful Mech."
    },
    {
      "type": "len_string",
      "start": 1235,
      "end": 2732,
      "length": 1495,
      "text": "Mounting a Clan Wolf-in-exile modified set of equipment.  This variation of the Wolfhound has more firepower than ever before.\r\n\r\nIt was designed with an experimental engine of the XXL variety, and the new XL Gyroscope.  Both of which have performed admirably in this mech.\r\n\r\nIt's new weaponry is all upgraded to an enhanced, light-weight, low-heat, Extended-Range Large Pulse Laser located on the left arm to complement the hand that is there.  Where the ER Large Laser use to be in the right arm, is now an ER PPC.  The three Medium Pulse Lasers that were on the front of the mech in the torso have been upgraded to the new ER Medium Pulse Lasers Variety.  As has the ER Medium Laser that was in the back of the mech.  The ECM Suite that was located in the head of the mech, has been upgraded to a variant on the Watchdog system with both ECM and Active Probe capabilities.\r\n\r\nDue to the innovation of the Clan Scientists and Techs that came with Khan Phelan Kell to Arc Royal and the innovation of Clovis Holstein and the NAIS.  The mech's armor, internal structure, and double heat sinks were not decreased in the slightest bit, despite the increase in firepower and range, as all the weapons are lighter and emit less heat than even the standard clan counterparts.  The biggest disadvantage to the new PPC design that is in use with this mech is the ability for someone who is looking at the weapon as it is fired will see the buildup of energy right at the barrel just before it is fired."
    },
    {
      "type": "len_string",
      "start": 2732,
      "end": 3663,
      "length": 929,
      "text": "This mech has yet to see an actual battle, although it has been tested against an entire star of warriors from Clan Wolf-in-exile and a lance of Kell Hounds, at the same time, during its testing phases.  All in all, this mech came through without much damage.  Able to make its attacks from a greater range than anybody predicted.  In the hands of Khan Phelan Kell it made short work of the Kell Hound lance that was pitted against it and proceded to take it's toll on the clan warriors.  The most amount of damage that the mech took was when it faced off against the mech piloted by Ranna Kerensky, as, has been pointed out to Khan Phelan in the past, she knows him almost better than he knows himself.  Certainly she knows him as well as he does.  But even with that knowledge, using a combination of Clan and Inner Sphere tactics, Khan Phelan won out against his opponents to prove that this mech definately has what it takes."
    },
    {
      "type": "len_string",
      "start": 3663,
      "end": 4103,
      "length": 438,
      "text": "Based off of the original clan variant for this Mech that was built by Ulric Kerensky to replace the one that was destroyed when Phelan was captured and made a bondsman while in the periphery.\r\n\r\nSince the original creation of this Mech, designed by Phelan's father and leader of the Kell Hounds, Morgan Kell, the following variants have seen action on the battlefield.\r\n\r\nWLF-1 Wolfhound\r\nWLF-2 Wolfhound\r\nWolfhound IIC\r\nWolfhound IIIC\r\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "ascii",
      "start": 4103,
      "end": 4104,
      "text": "/"
    },
    {
      "type": "byte",
      "offset": 4104,
      "hex": "00"
    },
    {
      "type": "ascii",
      "start": 4105,
      "end": 4152,
      "text": "Khan Phelan Kell, Clan Wolf-in-Exile; Grinner\r\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "len_string",
      "start": 4152,
      "end": 4635,
      "length": 481,
      "text": "Currently used by Khan Phelan Kell of Clan Wolf-in-Exile, and assorted scout lances both throughout Clan Wolf-in-Exile as well as the Wolf Dragoons and the Kell Hounds.  There are rumors that another Mercenary Unit has also aquired this design, to include the specs for everything on it (including weapons), and have at least one in operation.  These rumors have yet to be validated.  None of the other clans, the Great Houses of the Inner Sphere, or the new SLDF have this design."
    },
    {
      "type": "len_string",
      "start": 4635,
      "end": 5628,
      "length": 991,
      "text": "Initial Mech created using a design that I thoroughly enjoy playing with, just to see what all I could do with an already established design using a program as powerful as this.\r\n\r\nI created the Clan Wolf-in-exile custom weapons to outfit this mech.  It will probably never see action in any game unless it is one that is played between friends of mine and myself.\r\n\r\nBesides the Kell Hounds, Wolf's Dragoons, and Clan Wolf-in-exile, this mech is used by The Renegade Legion and hence Angel Squad which are two of my own Mercenary Units.  Angel Squad being the Command Company of The Renegade Legion.\r\n\r\nThis particular design has been set as a 3060 (I would have chosen something closer to 3065 except that option is not available <grin>) variant that is of Clan Tech base, however, the idea of having it worked on by Clovis Holstein as well as Clan Techs, gives it a true hybrid quality without mixing technologies.  Much the same as the pilot for whom it was design for, Khan Phelan Kell."
    },
